      {
        type: "application",
        title: "Bedside Application — Insulin Administration Bundle",
        content: `Every insulin dose follows a safety bundle. **Pre-dose**: verify order, check **glucose**, confirm meal status (rapid/regular = meal must be coming), look up sliding scale on POC result. **Independent double-check** with another RN — required by most facilities for insulin. **Drawing up**: clear before cloudy if mixing; **never** mix glargine. Use **U-100 insulin syringe** only. **Site rotation** prevents lipohypertrophy — abdomen (fastest), arm, thigh, buttock. **Injection**: 90° angle for SQ, no aspiration. **Document**: site, dose, glucose, meal intake. **Post-dose**: assess at **peak time** for hypoglycemia (NPH at 4–12 hrs, regular at 2–4 hrs). Teach the patient: **rotate sites**, **store unopened insulin in fridge**, **open vials at room temp for 28 days**, **never freeze**, carry **fast-acting carb** at all times. For sulfonylureas: **take with first bite of meal** — never on an empty stomach. Avoid **alcohol** (disulfiram-like reaction).`,
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="55" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="32" font-weight="bold">Insulin Safety Bundle</text><rect x="60" y="100" width="980" height="60" fill="#6366f1" rx="8"/><text x="550" y="140" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Every Dose · Every Patient · Every Time</text><rect x="60" y="180" width="320" height="240" fill="#ef4444" rx="8"/><text x="220" y="215" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Pre-Dose</text><text x="80" y="255" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">• Verify order</text><text x="80" y="285" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">• Check POC glucose</text><text x="80" y="315" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">• Confirm meal coming</text><text x="80" y="345" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">• Look up sliding scale</text><text x="80" y="375" fill="#ffd700" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">• Independent 2-RN check</text><text x="80" y="405" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">• High-alert medication</text><rect x="390" y="180" width="320" height="240" fill="#10b981" rx="8"/><text x="550" y="215" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Drawing Up</text><text x="410" y="255" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">• U-100 syringe only</text><text x="410" y="285" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">• Clear before cloudy</text><text x="410" y="315" fill="#ffd700" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">• Never mix glargine</text><text x="410" y="345" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">• Roll NPH gently (no shake)</text><text x="410" y="375" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">• Verify air bubbles cleared</text><text x="410" y="405" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">• Label syringe if not used</text><rect x="720" y="180" width="320" height="240" fill="#f59e0b" rx="8"/><text x="880" y="215" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Injection</text><text x="740" y="255" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="14">• Rotate sites</text><text x="740" y="285" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="14">• Abdomen fastest</text><text x="740" y="315" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="14">• 90° angle SQ</text><text x="740" y="345" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="14">• No aspiration</text><text x="740" y="375" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="14">• Hold 5 sec, remove</text><text x="740" y="405" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="14">• Don't rub site</text><rect x="60" y="450" width="465" height="200" fill="#8b5cf6" rx="8"/><text x="292" y="485" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Post-Dose Watch</text><text x="80" y="525" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15">• Document site/dose/BG</text><text x="80" y="555" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15">• Assess at peak time</text><text x="80" y="585" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15">• NPH peak: 4-12 hr</text><text x="80" y="615" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15">• Regular peak: 2-4 hr</text><text x="80" y="640" fill="#ffd700" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">• Fast carb at bedside</text><rect x="555" y="450" width="485" height="200" fill="#0ea5e9" rx="8"/><text x="797" y="485" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Storage Teaching</text><text x="575" y="525" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15">• Unopened: refrigerator</text><text x="575" y="555" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15">• Opened: room temp 28 days</text><text x="575" y="585" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15">• Never freeze</text><text x="575" y="615" fill="#ffffff" font-size="15">• Protect from light/heat</text><text x="575" y="640" fill="#ffd700" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">• Discard if cloudy (clear types)</text><rect x="60" y="680" width="980" height="170" fill="#ec4899" rx="8"/><text x="550" y="720" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">Sulfonylurea Teaching</text><text x="80" y="760" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">• Take WITH first bite of meal — never on empty stomach</text><text x="80" y="790" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">• Avoid alcohol — disulfiram-like reaction (flushing, N/V)</text><text x="80" y="820" fill="#ffd700" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">• HIGH hypoglycemia risk, especially in elderly</text><rect x="60" y="870" width="980" height="180" fill="#888" opacity="0.15" rx="8"/><text x="550" y="910" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">Patient Survival Skills</text><text x="100" y="950" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">• Carry fast-acting carb (glucose tabs, juice) at ALL times</text><text x="100" y="985" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">• Wear medical alert ID</text><text x="100" y="1020" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">• Know sick-day rules: check BG q2-4h, never skip insulin</text></svg>`,
          caption: "Insulin safety bundle from order verification through peak-time assessment, plus storage and sulfonylurea teaching."
        }
      }
