        explanation: `**Correct: Hold the morphine, stimulate, apply O2, notify provider.** An RR < 10/min is the universal threshold to hold opioid dosing. Giving more morphine (option 1) would worsen respiratory depression. Splitting the dose (option 3) is never within the nurse's scope. Naloxone (option 4) is reserved for unresponsive patients or when stimulation/O2 fail — stimulate first, then escalate. **Airway and breathing always come before pharmacologic reversal.**`,
