        content: `**Anemia patient assessment**: check **Hgb/Hct** trends, **MCV** (microcytic = iron, macrocytic = B12/folate, normocytic = chronic disease/aplastic), and clinical signs — pallor in conjunctivae and nailbeds, fatigue, exertional dyspnea, tachycardia. For **iron** therapy: take with **vitamin C**, on empty stomach if tolerated, expect **black stools** (not GI bleeding), use a **straw** for liquid iron to protect teeth. For **B12**: emphasize that injections are **lifelong** — oral B12 will not work without intrinsic factor.

**Sickle cell crisis** management spells **H-O-P** + warmth: **Hydration** (IV fluids), **Oxygen**, **Pain control** (often PCA morphine), warmth (cold causes vasoconstriction — worsens sickling).

**Bleeding-precaution patient**: avoid all unnecessary needle sticks, use a **soft toothbrush** (no flossing if platelets <20K), provide an **electric razor**, hold sites **at least 5 minutes** after labs, monitor **petechiae, ecchymoses, gum bleeding, hematuria, melena**. **Stool softeners** prevent straining (which can cause intracranial hemorrhage).`,
