        explanation: "**Frequent swallowing** is the #1 sign of post-tonsillectomy bleeding — blood drips down the throat and the child swallows it. Restlessness adds early shock signs. **Refusing red Popsicles is appropriate** (red liquids are avoided to prevent masking blood). Pain 4/10 is expected and treated with acetaminophen. **White exudate** in the surgical bed is the normal healing scab — not a complication.",
