        content: `**CF teaching plan for a newly diagnosed family**: enzymes with **every meal/snack** (capsule contents on cool applesauce, not formula or hot food), **CPT 2-4x/day** with huff coughing and flutter valve, daily **fat-soluble vitamins (ADEK)**, **high-calorie/high-fat** diet (CF kids need 110-200% RDA calories), **salt supplements** in hot weather. Annual flu shot. Report cough changes, weight loss, decreased appetite.

**Asthma action plan handout**: Green zone — daily controller (ICS), exercise freely. Yellow — add SABA q4h, contact provider if no return to green in 24 hr. Red — SABA + emergency care. Always use **spacer** under age 8. Rinse mouth after ICS.

**Tonsillectomy discharge**: Soft cool diet 1-2 weeks, **avoid red/brown liquids and straws**, acetaminophen for pain (no ASA/NSAIDs — bleeding risk), monitor for frequent swallowing or fresh blood — **call provider immediately**. Activity restriction 10-14 days. **Warn parents** about the day 7-10 scab separation window — this is when delayed bleeds happen.`,
