        type: "concept",
        title: "Day 1 Priorities — ABCs Then Safety",
        content: `**ABCs first, always**:
• **Airway/Breathing**: GCS 14, breathing OK, no aspiration
• **Circulation**: HR 108 (early withdrawal vs anxiety), BP 142/88
• **APAP toxicity**: 4h post-ingestion → draw **APAP level NOW** (peak), check **AST/ALT/INR/bilirubin baseline**, start **N-acetylcysteine (NAC)** loading dose 150 mg/kg over 1h, then 50 mg/kg over 4h, then 100 mg/kg over 16h (21-hour IV protocol)
• **Alcohol withdrawal**: last drink 16h ago, CIWA-Ar score 12 (moderate) → **lorazepam** 2 mg IV q1h PRN per CIWA, **thiamine 100 mg IV** BEFORE glucose (Wernicke prevention), folate, MVI

**Suicide safety** (parallel track, **NOT delayed**):
• **1:1 sitter** in line of sight at all times
• **Room search**: shoelaces, belts, cords, plastic bags, sharps removed
• **Suicide-proofed room**: weight-tested fixtures, no anchor points
• **Document**: 15-minute observation rounds + 1:1 sitter notes
• **Restraints**: chemical/physical only if behavioral emergency despite less restrictive options

**Lithium**: do **NOT restart** until medically stable + level drawn + renal function confirmed. **Hold** until cleared.`,
