      {
        type: "quiz",
        title: "Vent Alarm Priorities",
        question: "A patient on AC mode triggers a HIGH peak pressure alarm. The nurse's first action should be to assess for which of the following?",
        options: [
          { text: "Circuit disconnect at the wye connector", correct: false },
          { text: "Cuff leak around the endotracheal tube", correct: false },
          { text: "Obstruction such as biting the ETT, kinked tubing, or mucus plug", correct: true },
          { text: "Decreased respiratory rate set on the ventilator", correct: false }
        ],
        explanation: "**High pressure alarms = obstruction.** The nurse must rapidly assess for **biting the tube**, **kinked tubing**, **mucus plug requiring suction**, **coughing/bucking**, **bronchospasm**, or **pneumothorax**. **Circuit disconnect** and **cuff leak** trigger **LOW pressure** alarms (loss of pressure). A decreased rate setting is not the cause of an active alarm. Never silence the alarm without finding the cause — if unable to identify quickly, **disconnect and bag** the patient while troubleshooting.",
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="80" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="40" font-weight="bold">Alarm Direction Matters</text><rect x="50" y="150" width="490" height="450" rx="14" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="4"/><text x="295" y="200" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ef4444" font-size="28" font-weight="bold">HIGH Pressure</text><text x="295" y="240" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="22">= Obstruction</text><text x="80" y="290" fill="#ef4444" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Causes:</text><text x="80" y="325" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">• Biting ETT</text><text x="80" y="358" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">• Kinked tubing</text><text x="80" y="391" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">• Mucus plug</text><text x="80" y="424" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">• Coughing</text><text x="80" y="457" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">• Bronchospasm</text><text x="80" y="490" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">• Pneumothorax</text><text x="80" y="540" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Action: clear blockage</text><text x="80" y="572" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Suction, bite block</text><rect x="560" y="150" width="490" height="450" rx="14" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="4"/><text x="805" y="200" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="28" font-weight="bold">LOW Pressure</text><text x="805" y="240" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="22">= Leak / Disconnect</text><text x="590" y="290" fill="#0ea5e9" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Causes:</text><text x="590" y="325" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">• Circuit disconnect</text><text x="590" y="358" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">• Cuff leak</text><text x="590" y="391" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">• Accidental extubation</text><text x="590" y="424" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">• Loose connections</text><text x="590" y="457" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">• Chest tube leak</text><text x="590" y="540" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Action: trace circuit</text><text x="590" y="572" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Reconnect, recuff</text><rect x="50" y="640" width="1000" height="200" rx="14" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="3"/><text x="550" y="685" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">When in Doubt</text><text x="550" y="730" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="22">Disconnect and bag with BVM</text><text x="550" y="770" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">until problem identified</text><text x="550" y="815" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ef4444" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">NEVER silence alarms without cause</text><rect x="50" y="870" width="1000" height="160" rx="14" fill="#6366f1"/><text x="550" y="920" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">Pressure UP = something blocking</text><text x="550" y="970" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">Pressure DOWN = something leaking</text><text x="550" y="1010" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="22">Direction tells you the problem</text></svg>`,
          caption: "Up = blocked. Down = leaking. Direction guides action."
        }
      },
      {
        type: "application",
        title: "Bedside Vent Care",
        content: `Begin every shift with a **head-to-toe + ventilator check**: confirm **mode, rate, TV, FiO2, PEEP, peak/plateau pressures, alarms set**. Verify **ETT depth** at the lip and **cuff pressure 20-30 cmH2O**. Auscultate breath sounds bilaterally and confirm **ETCO2 waveform**. Maintain **HOB ≥30°** unless contraindicated. Perform **oral care q4h with chlorhexidine**, **subglottic suctioning** if available. **Suction only when indicated**: visible secretions, ↑peak pressures, ↓SpO2, restlessness. **Daily**: spontaneous breathing trial (SBT) to assess **readiness to wean** — uses PS or T-piece, observes for tachypnea, hypoxia, distress. **Sedation vacation** with SBT to assess neuro status. **Document** vent settings, ABG trends, lung sounds, suction output, and patient comfort/sedation score (RASS). When in doubt — **disconnect and bag** with BVM at 100% O2 while troubleshooting. Calm, systematic, vigilant.`,
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="60" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="38" font-weight="bold">Shift Vent Routine</text><rect x="50" y="120" width="1000" height="160" rx="12" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#6366f1" stroke-width="3"/><text x="550" y="160" text-anchor="middle" fill="#6366f1" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">Start of Shift Check</text><text x="100" y="200" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Mode, Rate, TV, FiO2, PEEP, alarms set</text><text x="100" y="235" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">ETT depth at lip + cuff 20-30 cmH2O</text><text x="100" y="270" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Auscultate + ETCO2 waveform</text><rect x="50" y="300" width="1000" height="160" rx="12" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="3"/><text x="550" y="340" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">Q4H Bundle</text><text x="100" y="380" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">HOB ≥30° verified</text><text x="100" y="415" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Oral care + chlorhexidine</text><text x="100" y="450" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Subglottic suction if available</text><rect x="50" y="480" width="1000" height="160" rx="12" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="3"/><text x="550" y="520" text-anchor="middle" fill="#f59e0b" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">Suction Only PRN</text><text x="100" y="560" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Visible secretions / ↑pressures</text><text x="100" y="595" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">↓SpO2 / restless patient</text><text x="100" y="630" fill="#ffd700" font-size="18">Avoid routine suction</text><rect x="50" y="660" width="1000" height="160" rx="12" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="3"/><text x="550" y="700" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b5cf6" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">Daily Wean Trial</text><text x="100" y="740" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Sedation vacation + SBT</text><text x="100" y="775" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">PS or T-piece trial</text><text x="100" y="810" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Monitor RR, SpO2, distress</text><rect x="50" y="840" width="1000" height="200" rx="12" fill="#ef4444"/><text x="550" y="890" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="28" font-weight="bold">WHEN IN DOUBT</text><text x="550" y="940" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">Disconnect → Bag at 100% O2</text><text x="550" y="990" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="22">Troubleshoot off the vent</text><text x="550" y="1025" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="20">Patient first, machine second</text></svg>`,
          caption: "Routine + readiness + rescue plan = safe ventilation."
        }
      }
