          svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="60" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="36" font-weight="bold">Delegation Decision Walk-Through</text><rect x="80" y="110" width="940" height="120" fill="#6366f1" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="2" rx="10"/><text x="100" y="145" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Stem: Assign 4 patients across RN, LPN (8 yrs), UAP (new)</text><text x="100" y="180" fill="#ffffff" font-size="17">Match acuity to scope. The most unstable patient stays with the RN.</text><text x="100" y="210" fill="#ffd700" font-size="17" font-style="italic">"Who is the most acute? Who is the most predictable?"</text><rect x="80" y="260" width="940" height="130" fill="#ef4444" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="2" rx="10"/><text x="100" y="295" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">A) UAP + new chest pain admission — REJECT</text><text x="100" y="325" fill="#ffffff" font-size="17">Wrong task: initial assessment is RN-only.</text><text x="100" y="355" fill="#ffffff" font-size="17">Wrong circumstance: unstable, awaiting troponin.</text><rect x="80" y="410" width="940" height="130" fill="#ef4444" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="2" rx="10"/><text x="100" y="445" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">B) LPN + IV vancomycin first dose — REJECT</text><text x="100" y="475" fill="#ffffff" font-size="17">Wrong task: initial-dose IV antibiotic carries anaphylaxis risk.</text><text x="100" y="505" fill="#ffffff" font-size="17">Trap: feels familiar from clinicals; NCLEX uses strict scope.</text><rect x="80" y="560" width="940" height="130" fill="#10b981" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="2" rx="10"/><text x="100" y="595" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">C) LPN + stable post-op day 2 — CORRECT</text><text x="100" y="625" fill="#ffffff" font-size="17">All 5 rights cleared: task, circumstance, person, direction, supervision.</text><text x="100" y="655" fill="#ffffff" font-size="17">Stable, predictable, within LPN scope.</text><rect x="80" y="710" width="940" height="130" fill="#ef4444" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="2" rx="10"/><text x="100" y="745" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">D) UAP + initial diabetic teaching — REJECT</text><text x="100" y="775" fill="#ffffff" font-size="17">Wrong task: initial teaching is RN-only, never delegable.</text><text x="100" y="805" fill="#ffffff" font-size="17">UAP can reinforce later, but not teach new content.</text><rect x="80" y="860" width="940" height="190" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="3" rx="10"/><text x="550" y="900" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">Rule: Most unstable / most unpredictable stays with the RN</text><text x="550" y="940" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">Initial assessments, initial teaching, IV pushes, blood, titrated drips,</text><text x="550" y="970" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">unstable patients — all RN.</text><text x="550" y="1015" text-anchor="middle" fill="#10b981" font-size="20" font-weight="bold">Answer: C</text></svg>`,
