        explanation: "Within 48 hours of an exam, NEW learning shows 30-40% lower retrieval than content allowed to consolidate during sleep (Karpinski, 2008). Marathon cramming (option 1) erodes sleep, spikes anxiety, and replaces consolidation with shallow encoding. Canceling (option 3) is rarely needed and creates more stress; a 62% score with identified weak patterns is workable. Skipping entirely (option 4) misses the chance to firm up weak rationales. The best move is targeted RATIONALE review of the 3 patterns today (no new questions), then a true rest day with cheat sheet + sleep on Day 2. Day 2's sleep is the critical consolidation night — protect it.",
