        type: "application",
        title: "Drill Plan: After Mock 7",
        content: `Run the same 90-minute structured drill as Mock 6, but with adjusted content focus.

**Block 1 (0–20 min) — Tag errors.** Same protocol: knowledge gap, test-taking, careless, or integration. Pay particular attention to ANY transfusion, anticoagulation, or anaphylaxis items. These have absolute rules — missing them suggests a deeper gap rather than a careless slip.

**Block 2 (20–50 min) — Algorithm review.** For each missed item, write out the FULL algorithm in order. Don't just write "anaphylaxis = epi" — write "epi 0.3 mg IM vastus lateralis q5–15min PRN → O2 → NS bolus → albuterol → diphenhydramine + famotidine → methylprednisolone → epi auto-injector script + MedicAlert + allergist referral." This rehearses the sequence under pressure.

**Block 3 (50–75 min) — Comparison tables.** Build (or rebuild from memory) these comparison tables: (1) Heparin vs warfarin vs DOACs, (2) UTI vs pyelonephritis, (3) BPH vs prostatitis vs prostate cancer, (4) HIV vs AIDS criteria, (5) Iron-deficiency vs B12 vs folate anemia, (6) AKI prerenal vs intrarenal vs postrenal. Comparisons drive NCLEX questions because they force discrimination between similar items.

**Block 4 (75–90 min) — Lab interpretation drill.** Look at 10 abnormal lab panels and identify the priority. Practice patterns: Hgb 6.8 + retic 12% = active hemolysis. INR 5.0 on warfarin = HOLD, vitamin K, monitor. K+ 6.8 + peaked T waves = STAT calcium gluconate + insulin/D50 + kayexalate. ANC 350 = neutropenic precautions, fever protocol. Platelets 18 = bleeding precautions, no IM injections.

**Key NCLEX safety rules to memorize cold.**
- Never bolus K+ IV push (always diluted, max 10 mEq/hr peripheral, 20 mEq/hr central).
- Never irrigate or remove dressings from new amputation/transplant without specific order.
- Never administer epinephrine SQ in anaphylaxis (IM only — faster onset).
- Never give live vaccines to immunocompromised patients.
- Never warm blood products in microwave (use blood warmer).

After completion: schedule Mock 8 within 72 hours. If you scored 70%+ on both Mocks 6 and 7, you are exam-ready and Mock 8 is the dress rehearsal. If below 65%, schedule one full content review day before Mock 8.`,
