        type: "intro",
        title: "The Final 48 Hours and What Comes After",
        content: `You are at the finish line. This is the final lesson of the NCLEX-RN preparation track — 10 books, 120 lessons, 600 cards, thousands of practice items. You have studied harder than 80% of test-takers who will sit alongside you on exam day. The remaining variable is execution: showing up rested, organized, calm, and confident. This lesson is your operational checklist for the 48 hours before the exam, the exam day itself, and the first 90 days of your nursing career.

**Exam logistics quick facts (Pearson VUE / NCSBN 2024):**
- Test windows: year-round, 7 days/week at most centers
- Check-in time: arrive 30 minutes before scheduled start
- Required ID: ONE acceptable government-issued photo ID with signature (passport, driver's license, military ID, state ID). Name must match the Authorization to Test (ATT) letter EXACTLY — middle initial, hyphens, spaces, suffixes all must match. Mismatches result in test cancellation and forfeit of the $200 exam fee.
- A second form of ID is recommended (credit card with name) as backup but not required.
- Biometric check-in: palm vein scan + signature + photo
- Personal items: ALL in locker. No phone, watch, jewelry beyond plain wedding band, food, water, gum, hat, sunglasses, jacket (must be left in locker — sweater allowed if pockets empty)
- Calculator: on-screen only, no physical calculator permitted
- Erasable whiteboard provided for scratch work
- Optional break after item 60 — proctor must re-check biometrics on return

**Results timeline:**
- Quick Results (unofficial): available 48 hours post-exam in 41 states for $7.95 via NCSBN/Pearson VUE
- Official results: released by your state board of nursing within 6 weeks (typical: 2-4 weeks; California historically slower at 4-6 weeks)
- License issuance: 1-7 business days after BON receives passing results, depending on state

You've earned this. Let's bring you home.`,
